---
import { COMPETITOR_HUB_PLATFORMS } from '@/lib/compare/alternativesHubData';
import { SAAS_MONTHLY_GBP } from '@/lib/seo/defaults';
---

<section class="alt-hub-section alt-hub-guide" aria-labelledby="alt-hub-guide-title">
  <div class="alt-hub__container alt-hub-guide__grid">
    <article class="alt-hub-guide__block">
      <h2 id="alt-hub-guide-title" class="alt-hub-section__title">How to choose booking software for your barbershop</h2>
      <p>
        There is no single best barber booking software for every UK barbershop. A self-employed barber,
        a growing five-chair shop and a multi-location business may need very different tools. Compare
        the total cost, brand control and day-to-day booking workflow against your actual needs — not
        just the cheapest advertised plan.
      </p>
      <ul class="alt-hub-guide__list">
        <li>
          <strong>Total monthly cost.</strong> Price the plan for your real team size. Some platforms charge per
          barber or calendar, others per location, and VAT may be added on top.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Commissions and processing fees.</strong> Check whether the platform takes a commission on any
          bookings, especially new clients from a marketplace, and compare card-processing rates separately.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking experience.</strong> Clients should be able to book in a few taps, see real availability and
          get confirmations and reminders.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Team size.</strong> Make sure the plan supports every bookable barber and the staff permissions you
          need.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Brand control.</strong> Decide whether clients should book on your own website and domain or inside a
          third-party app.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client data.</strong> Confirm how you can export your client list and booking history, and in what
          format.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deposits.</strong> Deposits and card-on-file policies reduce no-shows; check what each plan allows.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Switching.</strong> Ask what help is included to move clients, services and future appointments.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="alt-hub-guide__block">
      <h2 class="alt-hub-section__title">Marketplace bookings vs your own branded website</h2>
      <p>
        Marketplace apps can put your shop in front of people searching nearby, which can help a new or quiet shop
        fill gaps. The trade-off is that clients book inside someone else’s platform, next to other shops, and some
        marketplaces charge a commission when they introduce a new client.
      </p>
      <p>
        A branded website on your own domain keeps the booking journey, your reviews and your regulars under your
        name, and there is no marketplace commission to pay. You rely more on your own channels — Google, Instagram,
        QR codes and word of mouth — to bring clients in.
      </p>
      <p>
        Many shops use both: a marketplace for discovery and their own site for regulars. Full KERSIVO
        (£{SAAS_MONTHLY_GBP}/month per location) is built for the own-brand approach, with your website and standard
        domain included.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="alt-hub__container">
    <nav class="alt-hub-guide__links" aria-labelledby="alt-hub-all-comparisons">
      <h2 id="alt-hub-all-comparisons" class="alt-hub-guide__links-title">Every KERSIVO comparison</h2>
      <ul>
        {
          COMPETITOR_HUB_PLATFORMS.map((platform) => (
            <li>
              <a href={platform.href}>KERSIVO vs {platform.name}</a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
        <li><a href="/barber-software-cost-calculator">Barber software cost calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing">KERSIVO pricing</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
</section>
